  "notes": "COMMON PATTERNS:\nUsed as a suru verb. The pattern is ～に{精通|せいつう}する (to be well-versed in ~). The particle に marks the field or subject of expertise.\n- ～に{精通|せいつう}している (is well-versed in ~)\n- ～に{精通|せいつう}した + noun (noun well-versed in ~)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {法律|ほうりつ}に{精通|せいつう}する (to be well-versed in law)\n- {技術|ぎじゅつ}に{精通|せいつう}する (to be well-versed in technology)\n- {業界|ぎょうかい}に{精通|せいつう}する (to be well-versed in the industry)\n\nUSAGE:\nImplies deeper, more specialized knowledge than {詳|くわ}しい (knowledgeable). {精通|せいつう} suggests professional-level or expert familiarity.",
